  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "1837-root",
    "title": "New Article by Professor Jonas Otterbeck on Pop-Nashid",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "Professor Jonas Otterbeck has co-published a new article on pop-nashid",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "6c61d929f4aa52b9",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "1837-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/1837-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "New Article by Professor Jonas Otterbeck on Pop-Nashid"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "AKU-ISMC Professor, Jonas Otterbeck, professor of Islamic Studies, has co-published a new article entitled "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"Music Version\" versus \"Vocals-Only\": Islamic Pop Music, Aesthetics, and Ethics",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/03007766.2019.1581335",
                    "target": "_self",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " exploring the recent phenomena of pop-nashid. Looking at artists such as Maher Zain, Sami Yusuf and Harris J., the piece, co-written by musicologist Dr. Johannes Frandsen Skjelbo, analyses the historical development of different musical styles of pop-nashid, particularly the difference between 'vocals-only' and full instrumentation versions of the same songs.   "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Professor Otterbeck is set to publish a new book on the subject later this year.  In "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Awakening of Islamic Pop Music",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", he will expand on the history of nashid, Islamic discourse on popular music and the artists of the Islamic media company Awakening. "
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
